-- title:
--   Divisors of varpi^m in the crossing model are monomials
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e$ be a natural number with $1 \le e$. Write $R =$ `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)` for the quotient of the ring $W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ of formal power series in two variables (indexed by `Fin 2`) by the ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - C(\varpi^{e})$, and for $w \in W$ let `const (ϖ ^ e) w` denote the class of the constant series $C(w)$ in $R$. The theorem asserts: if $r \in R$ and $m$ is a natural number such that $r$ divides the $m$-th power of `const (ϖ ^ e) ϖ` in $R$, then there exist a unit $w$ of $R$ and natural numbers $a$, $b$, $n$ with $a = 0$ or $b = 0$ (equivalently $\min(a,b) = 0$) such that
--   $$r = w \cdot U(\varpi^{e})^{a} \cdot V(\varpi^{e})^{b} \cdot (\mathrm{const}\,(\varpi^{e})\,\varpi)^{n},$$
--   where `U (ϖ ^ e)` and `V (ϖ ^ e)` are the two distinguished elements of $R$ that play the role of the coordinates along the two branches.
--
--   This is the local structure statement for the crossing model $W[\![u,v]\!]/(uv-\varpi^{e})$ of a semistable double point: every divisor of a power of $\varpi$ is, up to a unit, a monomial $u^{a}v^{b}\varpi^{n}$ supported on at most one of the two branches. It is used by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_eq_unit_mul_U_pow_mul_V_pow_mul_const_pow_of_sInf_eq_sSup`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_eq_unit_mul_U_pow_mul_V_pow_mul_const_pow_of_sInf_eq_sSup), and the proof proceeds through the presentation of the model as an `AdjoinRoot` over a quotient of a one-variable power series ring, together with the principality and local structure of that quotient.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_eq_unit_mul_U_pow_mul_V_pow_mul_const_pow_of_dvd.lean

